    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Manager---Academic-Governance-Services_JR50640-2": {
      "title": "Manager – Academic Governance Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full time,   continuing position   HEW 9   (Starting from $141,417)   + 17% Superannuation     Based at the City campus plus flexible and hybrid working arrangements     About the position   The Manager, Academic Governance Services leads the development,   implementation   and continuous improvement of academic governance processes for vocational education (VE), associate   degree   and non-award offerings.   Drawing on strong   expertise   in VE,   HE   and non-award governance, you will provide strategic advice and coordinate activities across multiple teams to ensure programs   comply with   internal policies, regulatory   requirements   and quality standards. You will interpret legislation and governance frameworks, drive process improvements, and support the development of governance approaches across a range of domestic and international contexts.   As a senior leader within the Quality and Compliance team, you will   provide   expert guidance on governance pathways and compliance requirements, assess governance readiness, exercise delegated authority for governance actions, and support internal and external audit activities.   Working closely with Directors, Program Managers, the   CoVE   Partnerships   team   and key stakeholders across the University, you will support program approvals, amendments, transitions and discontinuations, oversee governance workflows and reporting, and help ensure academic quality and compliance across   CoVE's   portfolio.   This role requires exceptional stakeholder engagement, strong communication skills, and the ability to build collaborative relationships that support effective and compliant governance outcomes.   In this role, you will   Lead the review,   development   and implementation of academic governance processes and workflows across   CoVE .   Provide   expert advice on governance pathways, compliance   requirements   and program lifecycle activities, including approvals, amendments,   transitions   and discontinuations.   Ensure new and updated offerings   comply with   internal policies, external   regulations   and quality standards.   Assess governance readiness,   authorise   progression through governance processes and support sound decision-making.   Oversee governance workflows, reporting and risk management to support effective and compliant program governance.   Build strong collaborative relationships and   provide   trusted guidance to stakeholders across   CoVE   and the broader University.   Lead and support the Academic Governance team (currently two staff).     To be successful in this position,   you'll   bring   Significant experience   in academic governance, ideally within vocational education and/or higher education.   Strong knowledge of governance frameworks, regulatory   requirements   and quality assurance processes.   Demonstrated experience developing and improving governance processes,   policies   and workflows.   Exceptional communication and stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to influence,   collaborate   and prepare high-quality reports and governance documentation.   Strong analytical, problem- solving   and decision-making skills, with the ability to navigate complex environments and manage governance risks.   Proven ability to manage competing priorities, interpret data and deliver quality outcomes within tight   timeframes .     Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check.    About the   College of Vocational Educatio n   The next evolution in   V ocational   E ducation at RMIT will need to meet people where they are and take them where they want to go.   RMIT’s College of Vocational Education will be ready for the challenge, guided by the   EVOLVE@RMIT   Roadmap .    EVOLVE sets a bold agenda and reflects our ambition to   lead in   industry-connected, learner-centered education to deliver real-world impact.   The EVOLVE Roadmap will contribute to the overarching vision of RMIT’s Knowledge   With   Action Strategy and will support collaboration with stakeholders across colleges and portfolios while also maintaining a distinct VE focus to ensure we can shape the university’s future as a connected and future-facing vocational institution .     Our five Roadmap actions are:   Offer transformative education experiences to all students   Connect across RMIT and industry for applied research   Respond at pace and scale to industry,   government   and communities   Grow our impact as the leading multi-sector provider in our region   Invest in our people and   organisational   enablers to support our success   To Apply  Please   submit   your   CV   and   cover letter addressing   your interest and suitability   for this position by clicking on the ‘Apply’ link at the top of this page .     For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below   or contact   Medina   (Talent Acquisition)   at   medina.hubanic@rmit.edu.au .   Applications may be reviewed as they are received. We encourage interested candidates to apply as soon as possible, as RMIT reserves the right to close this advertisement prior to the closing date.   Position Description -   Manager, Academic Governance Services   Applications Close: 16 Sept 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
